{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1221,"ns":6,"title":"File:Earth-moon.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":995863,"width":3000,"height":2400,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Earth-moon.jpg/1280px-Earth-moon.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1024,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Earth-moon.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Earth-moon.jpg/1280px-Earth-moon.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1024,"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Earth-moon.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Earth-moon.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earth-moon.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=1221","extmetadata":{"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Earthrise|Great Images in NASA|Photographs taken on 1968-12-24|Photos taken with Hasselblad|Files from NASA with known IDs|Files from NASA on The Commons Flickr stream","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This view of the rising Earth greeted the Apollo 8 astronauts as they came from behind the Moon after the fourth nearside orbit. Earth is about five degrees above the horizon in the photo. The unnamed surface features in the foreground are near the eastern limb of the Moon as viewed from Earth. The lunar horizon is approximately 780 kilometers from the spacecraft. Width of the photographed area at the horizon is about 175 kilometers. On the Earth 240,000 miles away, the sunset terminator bisects Africa.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Apollo_8\" title=\"Apollo 8\">Apollo 8</a> crewmember <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Anders\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:William Anders\">Bill Anders</a>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},{"pageid":160807,"ns":6,"title":"File:Russia-CIA WFB Map--Tunguska.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":27952,"width":631,"height":321,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Russia-CIA_WFB_Map--Tunguska.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":651,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Russia-CIA_WFB_Map--Tunguska.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":651},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Russia-CIA_WFB_Map--Tunguska.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russia-CIA_WFB_Map--Tunguska.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=160807","extmetadata":{"Categories":{"value":"GFDL|License migration completed|Map images that should use vector graphics|PNG that should use vector graphics|Maps of Tunguska event","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"Map showing the approximate location of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunguska_event\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Tunguska event\">Tunguska event</a> of 1908.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"This is a hacked version of the public domain map <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russia-CIA_WFB_Map.png\" title=\"File:Russia-CIA WFB Map.png\">Russia-CIA WFB Map.png</a>.\n<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Bobby_D._Bryant\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:User:Bobby D. Bryant\">User:Bobby D. Bryant</a> made the modifications and uploaded it under the GFDL on May 21, 2005.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 3.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}]},{"pageid":357729,"ns":6,"title":"File:Solar system.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":4225968,"width":4500,"height":5600,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Solar_system.jpg/1280px-Solar_system.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1593,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Solar_system.jpg/3840px-Solar_system.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Solar_system.jpg/1280px-Solar_system.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1593,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Solar_system.jpg/3840px-Solar_system.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/83/Solar_system.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Solar_system.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=357729","extmetadata":{"Categories":{"value":"PD NASA|Solar System object comparisons|Files from NASA with known IDs","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This is  a montage of planetary images taken by spacecraft managed by the Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Pasadena, CA. Included are (from top to bottom) images of Mercury, Venus, Earth (and Moon), Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune. The spacecraft responsible for these images are as follows: \n<ul><li>the Mercury image was taken by Mariner 10,</li>\n<li>the Venus image by Magellan,</li>\n<li>the Earth and Moon images by Galileo,</li>\n<li>the Mars image by Mars Global Surveyor,</li>\n<li>the Jupiter image by Cassini, and</li>\n<li>the Saturn, Uranus and Neptune images by Voyager.</li>\n<li>Pluto is not shown as it is no longer a planet, and no spacecraft has yet visited it when this montage was taken. The inner planets (Mercury, Venus, Earth, Moon, and Mars) are roughly to scale to each other; the outer planets (Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, and Neptune) are roughly to scale to each other. PIA 00545 is the same montage with Neptune shown larger in the foreground. Actual diameters are given below:</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Sun\">Sun</a> (to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photosphere\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Photosphere\">photosphere</a>) 1,392,684 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mercury_(planet)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Mercury (planet)\">Mercury</a> 4,879.4 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Venus\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Venus\">Venus</a>                   12,103.7 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Earth\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Earth\">Earth</a>                  12,756.28 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moon\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Moon\">Moon</a>                     3,476.2 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Mars\">Mars</a>                     6,804.9 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jupiter\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Jupiter\">Jupiter</a>                  142,984 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saturn\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Saturn\">Saturn</a>   120,536 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uranus\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Uranus\">Uranus</a>                    51,118 km</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neptune\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Neptune\">Neptune</a>                   49,528 km</li></ul>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"NASA/JPL","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},{"pageid":516106,"ns":6,"title":"File:Crab Nebula.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":14508851,"width":3864,"height":3864,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crab_Nebula.jpg/1280px-Crab_Nebula.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1280,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crab_Nebula.jpg/3840px-Crab_Nebula.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crab_Nebula.jpg/1280px-Crab_Nebula.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":1280,"height":1280,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Crab_Nebula.jpg/3840px-Crab_Nebula.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/00/Crab_Nebula.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crab_Nebula.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=516106","extmetadata":{"Categories":{"value":"Crab Nebula|PD NASA|Images with annotations|Rayleigh–Taylor instabilities|Featured pictures from NASA|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, English|Hubble images of nebulae|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, German|Featured pictures of astronomy|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Chinese|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Persian|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Spanish|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Tamil|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Turkish|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Vietnamese|Featured photographs in the public domain|PD-USGov missing SDC copyright status|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Arabic|Files from Hubble Space Telescope Flickr stream|Files from NASA Goddard Space Flight Center Flickr stream","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"This is a mosaic image, one of the largest ever taken by NASA's Hubble Space Telescope, of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crab_Nebula\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Crab Nebula\">Crab Nebula</a>, a six-light-year-wide expanding remnant of a star's supernova explosion. Japanese and Chinese astronomers recorded this violent event in 1054 CE.\n<p>The orange filaments are the tattered remains of the star and consist mostly of hydrogen. The rapidly spinning neutron star embedded in the center of the nebula is the dynamo powering the nebula's eerie interior bluish glow. The blue light comes from electrons whirling at nearly the speed of light around magnetic field lines from the neutron star. The neutron star, like a lighthouse, ejects twin beams of radiation that appear to pulse 30 times a second due to the neutron star's rotation. A neutron star is the crushed ultra-dense core of the exploded star.\n</p><p>The Crab Nebula derived its name from its appearance in a drawing made by Irish astronomer Lord Rosse in 1844, using a 36-inch telescope. When viewed by Hubble, as well as by large ground-based telescopes such as the European Southern Observatory's Very Large Telescope, the Crab Nebula takes on a more detailed appearance that yields clues into the spectacular demise of a star, 6,500 light-years away.\n</p>\nThe newly composed image was assembled from 24 individual Wide Field and Planetary Camera 2 exposures taken in October 1999, January 2000, and December 2000. The colors in the image indicate the different elements that were expelled during the explosion. Blue in the filaments in the outer part of the nebula represents neutral oxygen, green is singly-ionized sulfur, and red indicates doubly-ionized oxygen.","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/NASA\" title=\"NASA\">NASA</a>, <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/ESA\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"ESA\">ESA</a>, J. Hester and A. Loll (Arizona State University)","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},{"pageid":838446,"ns":6,"title":"File:Wikisource-logo.svg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":16160,"width":410,"height":430,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Wikisource-logo.svg/1280px-Wikisource-logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":1280,"thumbheight":1342,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Wikisource-logo.svg/3840px-Wikisource-logo.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped